  // ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  overview: {
    lede:
      'Hamrash is a school management platform. Every school is an **organization**, every row of school data carries its `organization_id`, and Postgres row-level security makes sure people only ever see the schools they belong to. The apps are thin: the **database owns the rules**.',
    pieces: [
      { kind: 'FLUTTER · iOS AND ANDROID', name: 'Hamrash Admin', text: 'For the people who run a school: owner, admin, principal, vice principal and bursar. Sets up the calendar, classes, arms and subjects. Repo `hamrash-admin`.' },
      { kind: 'FLUTTER · iOS AND ANDROID', name: 'Hamrash Platform Admin', text: 'For the Hamrash team. Creates schools, hands owners their claim code, suspends or archives schools, manages the shared team code. Repo `hamrash-platform-admin`.' },
      { kind: 'SUPABASE · POSTGRES', name: 'The database', text: 'Project `ccvyhbyrtobdsecqvhcr`. Migrations, access tests and edge functions live in `hamrash-admin/supabase/`. Sign-in is Clerk (Apple or Google); the Clerk token is sent to Supabase, and `auth.jwt() ->> \'sub\'` is the caller.' },
      { kind: 'PLANNED', name: 'Teacher and parent apps', text: 'Not built yet. Roles `teacher`, `staff`, `parent` and `student` already exist in the database, and claim codes for them are turned away by Hamrash Admin without being used up.' },
    ],
    rules: [
      'A person can **sign in** to a school only through an `organization_members` row (a membership). What the school **knows** about them lives separately in `staff`, `students` or `parents`. A nursery pupil has a record but no login.',
      'Memberships start as **invites** with an 8-character claim code (`KQ7M-2X9B`). Redeeming the code in the app binds it to the person’s Clerk account and makes it `active`.',
      '**Leaders** (owner, admin, principal, vice principal) set up the school. The bursar mostly reads. Teachers, staff, parents and students have no admin-app access yet.',
      'A **suspended** or **archived** school hides all its data from its members straight away. Members can still see the school row and their own membership, so the app can show “This school is paused”. Nothing is deleted; schools are never deleted.',
      '**Private details** (date of birth, address, medical notes, parents’ email) sit in separate `*_private_details` tables with tighter read rules than the public profile.',
      'A **closed session** (last school year) is history: its terms, class teachers, placements, teaching assignments and subject choices can’t be changed or deleted. Only the owner can reopen it.',
      'Everything sensitive is a **security-definer function** in the `private` schema, which the Data API never exposes.',
    ],
    journey: [
      { title: 'Hamrash creates the school', text: 'A platform admin taps Add a school. `create_organization` makes the school in `trial` and an owner invite with a claim code.' },
      { title: 'The owner gets the code', text: 'The Platform Admin app shows the code once in a share sheet. It stays visible on the school page until it’s used.' },
      { title: 'The owner signs in to Hamrash Admin', text: 'Apple or Google through Clerk. With no membership yet, the app opens Join your school.' },
      { title: 'Check, then redeem', text: '`check_claim_code` shows the school and role without using the code. Join calls `redeem_claim_code`, which activates the membership and creates the owner’s staff record (`STF/0001`).' },
      { title: 'Confirm the school', text: 'First time only, the owner checks the school’s name, contact details, logo and number prefix and taps Looks good.' },
      { title: 'Set up from the Home checklist', text: 'Academic calendar → classes and arms → subjects → grading → Staff → Add students. Grading is “coming soon” in the app today; Staff opens the staff page; Add students opens the Add student wizard.' },
    ],
  },

